 "literal": "Great mountain descending pure white waterfall / rock cave reverberating many flowers mountain slope / small hamlet hill-tribe man large shoulders young girl / water like grace / fire like my strength of mind extinguished indeed",
 "translation": "On the mountain slopes rich with many flowers, where pure white waterfalls descend from the great peaks and reverberate in rock caves, lives the young girl with large shoulders, daughter of the hill-tribe man of the small hamlet. Her gentle grace is like cool water, yet it has completely extinguished my fire-like strength of mind.",
 "modern": "பெரிய மலையிலிருந்து இறங்கி வருகின்ற தூய்மையான வெள்ளை அருவி, பாறைக்குகைகளில் முழங்குகின்ற பல மலர்களைக் கொண்ட மலைச்சாரலில் உள்ள சிறு குடிலில் வாழும் குறவனுடைய பெரிய தோள்களைக் கொண்ட இளமகள், குளிர்ச்சியான நீரைப் போன்ற மென்மையான இயல்புடையவள். ஆனால், நெருப்பைப் போன்ற எனது மன வலிமையை அவள் முற்றிலும் அழித்துவிட்டாள்.",
 "explanation": "This poem is spoken by the hero to his companion, describing how his heart has been completely captured by the heroine. The setting is the mountainous Kuriñci landscape, characterized by roaring waterfalls, rocky caves, and slopes covered in diverse blossoms. The heroine is a young hill-tribe girl whose gentle grace is compared to cool, soothing water. In contrast, the hero's strong willpower and mental resolve are compared to fire. The central irony of the poem is that her water-like gentleness has completely extinguished his fire-like strength of mind, leaving him entirely helpless in love.",
